    "thesis": "MPC scores 62, a Hold, with no price data available, so valuation and trend did not count toward the score. Growth is the main support at a score of 90, driven by latest-quarter revenue growth of 53.8% year on year, TTM revenue growth of 15.0%, and growth that sped up by 45.3 pp from the previous quarter. Quality holds the score back at 44: refining margins are thin, with a gross margin of 12.5%, an operating margin of 9.2% and an FCF margin of 8.4%, partly offset by the diluted share count down 5.5% year on year. The balance sheet scores 54, with net debt at 1.94 times free cash flow and cash covering 0.24 of debt. News risk scores 54, helped by a run of broker price-target increases in October with no downgrades.",
    "key_risks": [
      "Refining margins could come under pressure as fuel prices fall, which would hit already thin operating and FCF margins.",
      "Families are suing over the August El Paso refinery release, and the El Paso air-permit renewal faces a contested-case hearing.",
